2) Check disk usage and alert if above 80%.
-->

#!/bin/bash

usage=$(df -h / | awk 'NR==2 {print $5}' | tr -d '%')

if [ "$usage" -gt 80 ]; then
    echo "Disk usage is high"
else
    echo "Disk usage is normal"
fi

>>>>>>>>

Filesystem      Size  Used Avail Use%
/dev/sda1        50G   40G   10G  80%
where,
NR → Current line number in AWK.
NR==1 → First line (header).
NR==2 → Second line (disk information).
$5 → Fifth column (Use%).
tr -d '%' → Removes %.


